# MoE host CPU compute tier: F2 static partition, replacing history-dependent LRU residency

# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of
# patches/0001-0017. Mechanism (DESIGN Section 7.0.2ae): the M9 equivalence gate's
# continuation check fails because the tier's expert-slot LRU is process-global and
# selects device-f16 vs host-f32 arithmetic by residency, so which experts are
# resident -- and therefore what a greedy decode step outputs -- depends on the
# request history in front of it, not just on the request itself. F2 replaces that
# LRU residency decision with a static partition: for each MoE layer, the resident
# set is the `slots` experts (the tier's own already-derived resident_slot_count())
# with the smallest splitmix64(seed, layer, expert) rank, fixed once at bind() time
# and independent of every subsequent request, dedup order, and pool-bytes budget.
#
# The earlier 0018 draft (F1: promote patch 0011's divergence oracle to a bit-equal
# host kernel, matching device f16 arithmetic exactly) was retired by review -- its
# file is not in this tree. F2 does not make host and device arithmetic agree; it
# makes the *set* of experts each arithmetic runs on a pure function of (seed,
# layer, expert, slots), so the mismatch F1 tried to erase no longer has an
# opportunity to depend on history at all.
#
# The rule (src/plugins/intel_gpu/src/graph/impls/ocl_v2/moe/static_partition.hpp,
# new file). splitmix64 (not std::hash, which is not guaranteed stable across STL
# versions or processes) mixes (seed, layer_key, expert) into a 64-bit rank key;
# static_partition_resident_experts(seed, layer_key, num_expert, capacity) ranks
# every expert in the layer and returns the `capacity` smallest, sorted by expert
# id -- ties broken by expert id, so the result is not std::sort-implementation-
# defined. layer_key is the layer's first OTD weight-file offset (the same
# structural per-layer key patches/0013's routing histogram already uses), not the
# process-order construction sequence, which is a run-to-run permutation (found in
# review for that patch). The vector's index for each expert IS its fixed device
# slot -- a pure function of the same four inputs, not of arrival order.
#
# The hook (expert_weight_providers.hpp/.cpp). OffloadExpertWeightProvider::bind()
# reserves the resident set into its LRUCache once, via a new reserve_pinned(expert,
# slot) that inserts at a caller-chosen slot number and marks it pinned -- before any
# real request reaches the provider. try_acquire_simultaneous() gains a third branch,
# static_partition_active (alongside the untouched cpu_tier_active LRU branch and the
# untouched tier-off branch): a resident expert resolves via LRUCache::probe() alone
# (present or not, no insertion, no eviction) to its fixed slot, filled on first use
# and never re-decided; a non-resident expert always takes the host tier and never
# enqueues an upload -- there is no warm-up/capacity-miss distinction, because
# occupancy was decided at bind(), not by arrival order. LRUCache gained a pinned bit
# per slot (m_pinned) that evict_one_unlocked() skips when choosing an eviction
# candidate, so prefill's ordinary (non-tier) acquisitions on the same shared pool
# can never evict a pinned slot; a pool where every slot is pinned throws loud rather
# than silently evicting a pin. patches/0017's readback path
# (on_before_batched_gemv's topk_id/x/rw hoist) is untouched by this patch.
#
# Bug #2, found and fixed in this tree: the prefill per-expert fallback path had no
# static-partition awareness. moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp's exec_prefill_onednn() calls
# on_load_expert_weights() once per expert in its own (non-batched, non-simultaneous)
# loop, which called IExpertWeightProvider::acquire_one() -- a second, independent
# entry point into the same shared LRUCache, untouched by the try_acquire_simultaneous
# rework above. Under the static partition every device slot is permanently pinned at
# bind() time (reserve_pinned(), all of it, none held back for ordinary LRU traffic),
# so evict_one_unlocked() has nothing left to reclaim: acquire_one()'s old
# unconditional get_lru_item() call threw at the first expert this loop met that was
# not in the resident set (LRUCache::evict_one: no evictable (unpinned) slot) --
# identical in kind to the decode-path bug F2 exists to fix, just reached from
# prefill instead of decode, and via a call site try_acquire_simultaneous's new
# static_partition_active branch never touches. Fixed by changing acquire_one's
# return type from a plain size_t to std::optional<size_t>, in the abstract interface
# (expert_weight_provider.hpp, singular -- IExpertWeightProvider) and both concrete
# providers (expert_weight_providers.hpp/.cpp, plural): ResidentExpertWeightProvider
# (device-only, no tier -- wraps its always-succeeds return in optional unchanged);
# OffloadExpertWeightProvider (the tier-aware one, expert_weight_providers.cpp) gains
# a static-partition branch mirroring try_acquire_simultaneous's probe()-only logic --
# a resident expert resolves to its fixed pinned slot (filling it on first use if
# bind()'s reservation pass has not already done so), a non-resident expert returns
# std::nullopt without touching the cache. The caller, on_load_expert_weights()
# (moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp, ~line 1358), now checks the optional and returns false
# instead of dereferencing a value that was never produced; exec_prefill_onednn()
# (~line 2924) reads that return as `resident` and only reads _dnnl_weights[expert_no]
# / runs the device oneDNN up/gate/down kernels when it is true. When false, the
# expert is not resident under the static partition and the loop takes a new host
# path in the same iteration -- not a skip, not a silent zero contribution: it reads
# back that expert's already-gathered scratch.x/scratch.routing_weights rows (the
# same f16-bit-pattern layout dispatch_cpu_tier's own hoisted readback already
# assumes), runs the existing moe_cpu_expert() host kernel (moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp's
# own decode-time CPU-tier capacity-miss path already calls the same function) per
# token for that expert, and copies the result back into scratch.y so index_add below
# treats it identically to a device-computed expert's contribution. cpu_tier_experts /
# cpu_tier_pairs perf counters are incremented for this fallback the same way the
# decode-time path already counts a host-tier expert. try_acquire_simultaneous()
# itself gained one more static-partition-aware branch alongside static_partition_
# active: calls that ask for grouped/batched acquisition but did not pass a
# cpu_tier_misses destination (on_before_prefill / build_grouped_mask_otd, neither
# wired for host-tier routing) now probe the partition and return std::nullopt on a
# capacity/non-residency miss -- the existing nullopt-lease contract both call sites
# already handle by falling back to exec_prefill_onednn's per-expert loop, which is
# what this bug fix makes safe to fall back into.
#
# This bug was not caught by review or by the unit tests below -- all four of this
# patch's own unit tests exercise LRUCache::reserve_pinned/probe/evict_one_unlocked
# with pinned_count < max_total (room left to evict from), not the 100%-pinned pool
# this bug needs to reproduce (the tier's real slot pool is entirely reserved by
# bind()'s pass, by construction -- resident_slot_count() experts pinned into a pool
# sized to exactly resident_slot_count()). It was found by attempting a real load
# under the intended production configuration (--offload-ratio 50 --moe-cpu-tier,
# 35B, GPU.1, u8 paged KV) and reading the crash it produced against this bug's own
# description above -- not by a unit test that was red before the fix and is green
# after it. That gap is recorded here rather than closed by a unit test that does not
# exist yet: a fifth moe_3gemm_static_partition case reproducing a 100%-pinned pool
# and exercising acquire_one() (not just probe()/get_lru_item()) directly is owed
# before this patch should be considered to have proportionate unit coverage for bug
# #2, on top of the live-hardware coverage below.
#
# The property and env. MOE_CPU_TIER_STATIC_PARTITION (properties.hpp, options.inl):
# a read-only bool property, true by default, reporting whether the F2 rule is in
# effect. Its default is computed once per ExecutionConfig construction from
# MOE_CPU_TIER_PARTITION (the same per-instance env-read idiom patches/0013 already
# established for MOE_OTD_ROUTING_HIST): MOE_CPU_TIER_PARTITION=lru sets the default
# false, restoring the pre-F2 LRU path byte-for-byte (cpu_tier_active branch,
# unedited). moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp's constructor re-reads the same env var
# directly as a second, redundant guard (in case a config object was built before the
# var was set) and wires OffloadExpertWeightProvider::set_static_partition(). Not
# added to plugin.cpp's settable-property list -- registered like moe_cpu_tier and
# moe_cpu_tier_threads, but genuinely read-only, never user-set. The `cpu_tier on:`
# OTD_PERF log line gains static_partition=0|1, seed=0x<kStaticPartitionSeed>, and
# resident_checksum=0x<FNV-1a of the resident set> (0 when the LRU path is in
# effect), so two runs' logs can be diffed for residency agreement without dumping
# the whole set.
#
# Bug #1, found this session, fixed in arcint (backend_ov.cpp, not this patch's own
# files): the expert-slot device-pool sizing logic (Phase B of arcint's own fit
# ledger) sizes the pool by a plateau probe that saturates it by observing EVICTION
# -- it feeds distinct-token chunks until the device-resident byte count stops
# growing, which relies on the driver evicting a cold slot to make room for a new
# one. Under a 100%-pinned static partition no slot is ever evictable by
# construction (that is the whole point: it is what makes output history-
# independent), so every probe chunk drove LRUCache::evict_one_unlocked() into its
# "no evictable (unpinned) slot" throw and the load died before reaching the rest of
# Phase B. First fixed (2026-09-04) by reading the same MOE_CPU_TIER_STATIC_
# PARTITION property (below) once the model is compiled and skipping the probe
# when it is true, pricing the device term analytically instead (the pinned pool's
# full size). The 0.3.0 release gate (2026-09-05, arcint DESIGN Section 7.0.2ai)
# showed that ceiling is the wrong ADMISSION charge on the 16 GiB card: the driver
# keeps most of the pinned pool host-mapped there, the LRU probe had read 0.11 GiB
# of VRAM for the same 7.50 GiB pool, and charging 7.50 refused a configuration
# the card serves. Final fix, arcint-side: the plateau probe runs under the static
# partition as well -- with bug #2 (below) fixed, non-resident experts take the
# host tier without an upload and nothing evicts, so the probe saturates as the
# pinned set fills on first use -- the analytic ceiling is only the fallback when
# the probe throws, and is logged beside the probe's reading as a cross-check
# (arcint logs "source: probe-static" for the measured figure, "static" for the
# fallback).
#
# Bug #3, found by this session's first gate run, fixed in arcint (backend_ov.cpp,
# not this patch's own files): the plugin-side fix above (bug #2) is real and
# measured -- a clean load under --offload-ratio 50 --moe-cpu-tier (no
# --prefix-cache-mib) serves a real completion, and the 4 unit tests below pass --
# but the M9 equivalence gate's actual target scenario, patch 0018's own reason to
# exist, is --moe-cpu-tier together with --prefix-cache-mib > 0, and that
# combination refused at load on the first attempt, never reaching decode, let alone
# the continuation-restored-from-cache check DESIGN Section 7.0.2ae exists to
# re-measure. Root cause, measured (backend_ov.cpp ~line 2678, not this patch's own
# files): arcint's --prefix-cache-mib refusal gate read the property with
# `core_.get_property(device, "MOE_CPU_TIER_STATIC_PARTITION")` -- a pre-compile,
# Core/device-level query, the same shape as the working PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_
# PARTITIONS probe it was modelled on (backend_ov.cpp's own comment said so). That
# probe works because paged_attention_max_partitions is registered in plugin.cpp's
# device-level property list (confirmed: `ov::PropertyName{...paged_attention_max_
# partitions..., PropertyMutability::RW}`, plugin.cpp:817) in addition to compiled_
# model.cpp's per-compiled-model list. moe_cpu_tier_static_partition (this patch's
# compiled_model.cpp hunk, unchanged from the original 0018 draft) is registered
# ONLY in CompiledModel::get_property() -- never added to plugin.cpp's device-level
# list, exactly as this header already documented ("not added to plugin.cpp's
# settable-property list... genuinely read-only"), but that same omission means
# `core_.get_property(device, ...)` has nothing to find before a model is compiled:
# it threw, the catch folded that to `static_partition_reported = false`, and
# tier_prefix_cache_decision (config.cpp) kept the F0 refusal exactly as if this
# patch did not exist. Measured server log, this session, GPU.1, this exact m18
# build, first attempt: "could not bring up the OpenVINO executor: --moe-cpu-tier
# with --prefix-cache-mib > 0 violates DESIGN Section 3.4: ... the plugin does not
# report a static residency partition". Fixed by moving the refusal's property read
# from `core_` (pre-compile) to `paged_model_` (the just-compiled model, the only
# point this plugin fact is actually knowable) -- the same read Bug #1's probe-skip
# logic above already needed and already gets right; the two now share one
# `static_partition_reported` local instead of the working call site and the broken
# one disagreeing. A later review pass (2026-09-04, before commit) found this
# refusal was reachable only from inside `if (!forced)` -- ARCINT_FIT_SLOT_BYTES
# (an experiment-only env override of the device-pool sizing, arcint-side) could
# skip Bug #1's and Bug #3's fixed code path entirely and load
# `--moe-cpu-tier --prefix-cache-mib > 0` against a non-static (LRU) plugin with no
# refusal at all -- fixed by hoisting the property read and the refusal out of that
# branch, arcint-side, so it always runs whenever --moe-cpu-tier is on regardless of
# how the slot pool ends up sized. The same review pass added a refusal for the
# companion gap: a static partition that priced the device term at 0 bytes (an
# unfound MoE shape, not an actually-empty pool) used to load silently; it now
# refuses loudly instead of charging the budget nothing for a pool the plugin is
# demonstrably filling.
#
