#   - `on_load_expert_weights`'s false return is genuinely overloaded (OTD off
#     entirely vs. not-resident under this patch's static partition) and its
#     one caller (exec_prefill_onednn, the fix above) does not distinguish
#     them -- on a NON-offloaded (resident-only) load reaching that caller, it
#     would `static_cast<OffloadExpertWeightProvider*>(_weight_provider.get())`
#     on a `ResidentExpertWeightProvider*`, undefined behaviour. Traced every
#     path that can reach exec_prefill_onednn (on_before_batched_gemv,
#     on_before_prefill, build_grouped_mask_otd's own fallback, and the
#     top-level dispatch's plain else) -- the first three all explicitly check
#     `_weight_provider->is_offloaded()` before ever calling it, so the
#     dangerous case is reachable only through the top-level else, which is
#     reachable only when MOE_USE_GROUPED_GEMM_PREFILL is forced off (default
#     true, arcint never touches it) -- dormant in every configuration arcint
#     actually drives today, not exercised, not fixed.
#   - The blocking `scratch.x`/`scratch.routing_weights` `copy_to` calls in the
#     same fallback have no explicit wait on the gather kernel's own event, but
#     both the gather (via execute_stage) and the copy_to share one stream
#     (`instance.get_network().get_stream()`), and that stream is forced
#     in-order whenever oneDNN is in use (execution_config.cpp: `if
