+// arcint F2 (patch 0018, DESIGN Section 7.0.2ae). splitmix64: a small, fast,
+// well-distributed 64-bit mix, used here (not std::hash, which is
+// implementation-defined and not guaranteed stable across STL versions or
+// even across processes of the same binary for integer keys on some
+// standard libraries) so the resident set is bit-reproducible: the same
+// (seed, layer, expert) triple ranks the same way on every process, every
+// build, every day. That reproducibility is the entire property F2 exists
+// to buy back after F1 (a bit-equal host kernel) was retired by review --
+// F2 does not make host and device arithmetic agree; it makes the *set* of
+// experts that take each arithmetic a pure function of (seed, layer,
+// expert, slots), so a greedy decode no longer depends on the LRU's request
+// history (DESIGN Section 7.0.2ae: the M9 continuation-check fork).
+inline uint64_t splitmix64(uint64_t x) {
+    x += 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15ULL;
+    uint64_t z = x;
